      "writtenOn": "2022-05-10T09:11:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) The whole idea about the reconnection policy came up in the context of group operations. The idea was to try reconnecting to group members who have disconnected, to keep the group in a consistent state. One problem here is that to my knowledge we are not getting any disconnection reason via disconnection callback. So the idea is to reconnect always, unless the users choice about the connection policy forbids (checking okToConnect()).\n\nI\u0027m just wondering if we should really involve groups here, or reconnect regardless the group information being available or not. If we should do that only for groups, then the disconnection event needs to be propagated to the service and the decision should be made there.\n\nI\u0027m also not sure if we should stop reconnecting if all the grouped devices disconnect.\n\n2) I believe the background connection should involve less resources as it should be using the allowed device list in the controller so it should autoconnect once the peer device becomes available.",
